x-Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"370\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg/500px-Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1894\" data-file-height=\"2800\"></a><figcaption>Name and title of Ulugh Beg on the canopy over the ruler.(<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/artofpersiancour0000soud/page/70/mode/1up?view=theater\">Art of the Persian courts\u00a0: selections from the Art and History Trust Collection p.70</a>) </figcaption></figure>\n<p>Ulugh Beg with ladies of his harem and retainers, Timurid 1425-50, Freer and Sackler Galleries\n</p><p><br>\n</p>\nReference: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/womeninmedeivali0000unse/page/214/mode/2up?view=theater\">Women in the medieval Islamic world\u00a0: power, patronage, and piety, p.215</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"between 1425 and 1450<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1450-00-00T00:00:00Z/7,P1319,+1425-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1450-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"197864546":{"pageid":197864546,"ns":6,"title":"File:Ulugh Beg's wine tankard (mashrabeh), about 1417-49 CE, Herat or Samarkand.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":31931,"width":736,"height":920,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Ulugh_Beg%27s_wine_tankard_%28mashrabeh%29%2C_about_1417-49_CE%2C_Herat_or_Samarkand.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":2000,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Ulugh_Beg%27s_wine_tankard_%28mashrabeh%29%2C_about_1417-49_CE%2C_Herat_or_Samarkand.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":2000},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Ulugh_Beg%27s_wine_tankard_%28mashrabeh%29%2C_about_1417-49_CE%2C_Herat_or_Samarkand.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulugh_Beg%27s_wine_tankard_(mashrabeh),_about_1417-49_CE,_Herat_or_Samarkand.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=197864546","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Ulugh Beg's wine tankard (mashrabeh), about 1417-49 CE, Herat or Samarkand\nIn the Calouste Gulbenkian Museum, Lisbon. This tankard connects the Mughal emperors directly to their Timurid ancestors. It belonged to Timur's grandson, Ulugh Beg (1394-1449), whose title forms the main calligraphic decoration. Nearly 200 years later, it was presented to Jahangir. His title and the Persian verses on the rim were almost certainly added by Saida Gilani, the multi-talented Iranian supervisor of the Mughal goldsmiths. He may also have made the handle. When Jahangir's son Shah Jahan inherited the precious dynastic heirloom, Sa'ida added his imperial title below the handle.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2026-08-20","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:SpeakingArch\" title=\"User:SpeakingArch\">SpeakingArch</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"130195823":{"pageid":130195823,"ns":6,"title":"File:Ulugh Beg, Timurid painting 1425-50.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":2723895,"width":1413,"height":1890,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/Ulugh_Beg%2C_Timurid_painting_1425-50.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":2140,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/Ulugh_Beg%2C_Timurid_painting_1425-50.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":2140},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/Ulugh_Beg%2C_Timurid_painting_1425-50.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulugh_Beg,_Timurid_painting_1425-50.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=130195823","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nUnknown artist<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown artist</span></div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg/250px-Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"370\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg/500px-Name_and_title_of_Ulugh_Beg_on_the_canopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1894\" data-file-height=\"2800\"></a><figcaption>Name and title of Ulugh Beg on the canopy over the ruler.(<a rel=\"nofollow\"